merecat (3.00~rc2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release candidate.  Notable changes since v2.31:
    - Support for HTTPS, self-signed certs and Let's Encrypt.  Works with
      all features, including virtual hosts.  Requires OpenSSL >= 3.0
    - Verify HTTPS certificate validity at startup, refuse to start if a
      certificate has expired or is not yet valid; new -k option overrides
    - Support for running multiple servers from one Merecat daemon,
      e.g. HTTP and HTTPS, or different ports
    - Reverse proxy support (proxy-pass) with path prefix rewriting and
      Location/Refresh header rewriting (proxy-redirect), like nginx
    - Support for HTTP redirect, e.g. from HTTP to HTTPS
    - Support for server location directive, similar to nginx
    - Support for HTTP/1.1 keep-alive
    - Support for HTTP gzip compression, also serves .gz files
    - Support for SSI, pattern matching to .shtml files
    - Support for PHP, using php-cgi
    - CGI setenv: inject custom environment variables into CGI programs
    - Built-in icons for dir listings, and a cute cat favicon
    - Allow SO_REUSEPORT, useful for load balancing
    - Linux performance: epoll, sendfile, TCP_NODELAY
  * Notable fixes:
    - Fix TLS handshake blocking the event loop, could stall the server
    - Fix missing access log entries for successful (200) file responses
    - Fix empty POST body in CGI when running as daemon (fd 0-2 reuse)
    - Fix issue with leading double slash in URL, reported by Steve Kemp
    - Fix 403 instead of 404 for missing files and dot-file probes
    - Fix HTML entities in directory listings
    - Cache-Control header fixes, no longer caches error responses
    - htpasswd tool hardening: overflow, EOF hang, temp file handling
    - IPv6 fallback: continue with IPv4 when IPv6 socket is unavailable
  * Packaging: use ~rc versioning so the final 3.00 upgrades cleanly over
    release candidates (3.00-rc1 sorted higher than 3.00-1)

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:54:33 +0200


